,"following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/arkology/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-03T19:10:43Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T19:10:43Z","body":"And this is the reason why I abandoned 2 similar PRs :) Too complicated.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5530796042/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5531116527","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123128#issuecomment-5531116527","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123128","id":5531116527,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABSa4j7w","user":{"login":"45DegreeAngl","id":154566159,"node_id":"U_kgDOCTZ-Dw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/154566159?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl","html_url":"https://github.com/45DegreeAngl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-03T19:38:00Z","updated_at":"2026-09-03T19:50:49Z","body":"So here's what I have so far:\r\n<img width=\"1100\" height=\"371\" alt=\"Progress\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a9e20e6a-616f-41e0-803c-4fe5a699b6aa\" />\r\n\r\nAssume that A has its atlas set to Source, B has its atlas set to A and C has its atlas set to B\r\n\r\nThe issue im having is determining what intended behavior for margins of a nested atlas texture even would be\r\nIt just seems that margins should be done at the lowest level of a nested atlas texture, not like in the middle of it because what is the point of the region if the entire size of the image is going to be adjusted on the fly\r\n\r\n(and I read somewhere that nesting texture atlases is not intended behavior but personally I really like the ability to have a large image of sprites and have atlas texture do the heavy lifting of segmenting that spritesheet and then if I want a specific region of that spritesheet as a texture instead of having to do the math or using sprite2d and counting the frames, having it as an atlas texture is kinda the whole point)\r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5531116527/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5557566367","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123128#issuecomment-5557566367","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123128","id":5557566367,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABS0G7nw","user":{"login":"45DegreeAngl","id":154566159,"node_id":"U_kgDOCTZ-Dw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/154566159?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl","html_url":"https://github.com/45DegreeAngl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/45DegreeAngl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-06T06:51:32Z","updated_at":"2026-09-06T06:53:09Z","body":"Should the margins be considered per region of an atlas or should margins not apply at all for the representation of the texture atlas but only applied to the final texture output?\n\nBasically if I have Source, A,B,C. A,B,C are atlas textures with margins mA,mB,mC.\nA->Source, B->A,C->B.\n\nWhen displaying B, do I just display the region of texture A without considering mA? And then after getting the region apply mB?\n\nDo the margins stack or is it only the top layer?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5557566367/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]